    {
      "id": "ROUT-F006",
      "severity": "high",
      "title": "Pruned minimum search omits repairs outside unstated engine preconditions",
      "finding": "The two-instance pruning retains only deltas mentioning the target. A reachable rule-free base with six data, one unary form, instance(0,[0]), existing requirements(2,3),(4,5), and already-separated target(0,1) has four valid two-instance repairs that mention no target endpoint. No cost0/1 response works and no pruned cost2 response works, so the displayed min_responses algorithm returnsNone although the declared full space contains repairs. Engine use may maintain stronger invariants, but the public API validates only rule-freedom and max_items.",
