    {
      "id": "ROUT-F009",
      "severity": "medium",
      "title": "Boundary replay loses supply provenance across chunk boundaries",
      "finding": "A Supply(x) prefix leaves BRegime unchanged. A later AdmitMark(x) suffix is rejected when replayed from that state, although the concatenated history succeeds. supplied is local to each replay call. This differs from the state-only fold contract of the main kernel; the boundary API must carry provenance or state its whole-history requirement.",
