      "assessment": "All887 quantum-lattice lines read in three contiguous chunks.",
      "limitations": "Product state/term constructors implement useful finite physical premises and full incident g instead of isolated edge g; signed comparison exposes vacuous negative bounds. Public term packets bypass one/two-locality and Hermiticity checks because lattice validator rechecks only IDs, sites and shapes. Public lattice fields remain mutable. Finite t can overflow RHS to negative infinity and produce a green comparison. Numerical fixture tests are source only, no native/physical certification.",
